WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:09.870
Mexico is in fashion in Hollywood.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.800
While Donald Trump
keeps trying to build the wall at the southern

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.420
border,
Mexican movie directors have won 5 of the

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.570
past 6 Oscars
for best director.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:21.789
But, as talented as Mexicans are in the film
industry, they are far less lucky when it

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:27.279
comes to politics.

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:29.509
A
year ago, we told you how the country of Guillermo

00:00:29.509 --> 00:00:33.440
del Toro
ended years of bipartisan politics that lead

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.720
to rampant
corruption.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.210
For a better understanding, the country’s
latest

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:40.200
president, Enrique Peña Nieto, left office
with the worst

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.370
ratings any Mexican president has ever had.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.370
And this is how the new president began his
term.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.150
Of
course, we’re talking about ANDRES MANUEL

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.760
LOPEZ
OBRADOR, also known as AMLO, the new Mexican

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:51.780
left-
wing rockstar.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.740
He is the first president to win more than
30

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:55.740
million votes.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.440
That’s a landslide victory.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.740
And it’s even more
surprising if we take into account that he

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:06.820
didn’t come from
either of the two major political parties.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.530
Mexicans wanted a
radical change and that’s exactly what AMLO

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.530
promised.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.819
The question now is… is he delivering?

00:01:12.819 --> 00:01:14.229
And Xander is going to give us the answer.

00:01:14.229 --> 00:01:16.320
And Erik is going to give us the answer.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.460
Truth be told… yes, things are changing
in Mexico.

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:21.710
They
are changing for the worse.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:25.889
Their GDP growth rate was 2%
in 2018, but in 2019, they’re only projected

00:01:25.889 --> 00:01:27.250
to grow about
0.2%.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:30.619
Yes, so far it seems like Mexico is heading
towards a

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:31.759
recession.

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:33.350
And yes, yes, I know what you’re thinking…

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.350
Come on,
Simon!

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.860
The brand new Mexican president hasn’t even
been

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.950
in office for a year.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.850
Can we really blame him for what’s
going on in the country?

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.299
Today, we are going to answer to

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:42.299
this question.

00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:44.479
But before we do, let’s take a look back
at the

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:47.509
history.

00:01:47.509 --> 00:01:52.560
THE REVENANT
Yes, I’m sure many of you have watched that

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.560
movie.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.219
‘The
Revenant’s Mexican director, Alejandro González

00:01:55.219 --> 00:01:58.249
Iñarritu,
won his second Oscar for best director with

00:01:58.249 --> 00:01:59.249
this film.

00:01:59.249 --> 00:02:01.010
But the
real revenant in this story is AMLO.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.409
He started his career as
a member of one of those two big Mexican political

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:07.620
parties:
The Institutional Revolutionary Party, also

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.030
known as PRI.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.240
This used to be the country’s big center-left
party.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.790
But
AMLO soon realized that this party wasn’t

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:16.350
far enough to the
left for him.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.890
So he created his own spin-off that led him
to

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:23.790
become the Mayor of Mexico City.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.970
This is how AMLO became famous nation-wide.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:29.990
Then, in
2006, he ran for President but lost by 250,000

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:31.080
votes.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.170
Instead of accepting the result, AMLO started
several

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.950
protests and his supporters claimed he was
the legitimate

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:37.950
president.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.020
Then he ran for president again in 2012, with
even worse results.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.930
At the time, it seemed like his career
was over.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.000
Yes, nobody would invest a penny in AMLO´s
future.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.280
But
then, against the odds, he rose from his ashes

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.340
with a brand
new political party: MORENA.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.690
His program was very simple:
destroy everything the previous administrations

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.810
had done in
Mexico and start from scratch.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:03.520
And oh boy!

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:09.790
In a country as
corrupt politically dysfunctional, and poverty-stricken

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.900
as
Mexico, this formula couldn’t have worked

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:13.900
better.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:14.900
And let’s be honest here…

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:15.900
AMLO isn’t disappointing
anyone.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.510
You see, in Mexico, after winning the elections,
you have to

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.610
wait 5 months before you really start being
the president.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:23.890
During this time, the would-be president just
waits.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:27.410
But
AMLO used this 5 months to hold lots of referendums.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.620
His
idea was that, as soon as he started his term,

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.130
he would
already have a list of popular policies ready

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.130
to be
implemented.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:34.680
And now you might say, Oh!

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.230
That doesn’t seem like a bad
idea, right?

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:41.210
You guys at VisualPolitik have already praised
direct democracy in countries like Liechtenstein

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:42.310
and
Switzerland!

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:48.950
So you must be big AMLO fans!

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:52.940
Yes, you’re right, referendums can be pretty
cool.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:56.040
But they
must have guarantees and be organized by the

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.040
government.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:01.190
When a political party organizes referendums
by themselves without any controls, it’s

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.190
usually a joke.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:05.210
And
this is exactly what AMLO has been doing.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.819
For most of these referendums, only 1 out
of 5

00:04:07.819 --> 00:04:10.990
municipalities actually had voting cabins.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:14.319
And the elections were so rigged that… that…
well… just

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:17.199
look at this news!

00:04:17.199 --> 00:04:22.090
A person could vote 4 times on the referendum
about the

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.560
new airport
But this is not the end of the story!

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:28.150
You see, when we talk
about referendums, the way we write the question

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.590
can have
a big impact on the outcome.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:33.840
In other words, if you change
the wording, you can easily manipulate the

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.840
result.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:35.840
For
example, if I ask…

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:37.690
“Do you agree with increasing old
people’s pensions?”

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.930
Or “Do you want a better healthcare
system?”

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.090
I’m sure most of you would say YES.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.150
Well… these
were the kinds of questions people from the

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.310
MORENA party
asked.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.930
And how many citizens voted?

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:51.030
Most of the
referendums had a turnout lower than 1%---about

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:54.470
equal to
the percentage of absolute die-hard AMLO supporters.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:57.340
And,
of course, all these policies had more than

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:04.540
90% approval
ratings.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.800
Of course, none of these referendums had any
legal

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:07.800
backing.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.660
But they have been the perfect way for AMLO
to

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.040
justify all his decisions.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:12.630
At the end of the day, Hey!

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.720
He’s just
doing what the citizens want!

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.400
And now you might wonder… what kind of decisions
is

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.400
AMLO making?

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.610
Here’s an example!

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:22.680
Cancelling the
construction of Mexico City&amp;#39;s New International

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:23.680
Airport.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.040
We
don’t know if the Project was good or bad.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:28.840
But the truth is it
costs 13 billion dollars of which 5 billion

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.130
were already spent.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:33.850
So basically, Mexico has just thrown 5 billion
USD out the

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:34.850
window.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:35.850
And you might wonder…

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.230
Why did he do that?

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:38.230
Easy!

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.590
One of those referendums, where only 1% of
the

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:42.770
population voted, said that the public agreed
with cancelling

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:43.770
construction.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:45.990
In a way, you can argue that many other politicians
base

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.580
their policies on polls.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:52.830
But the difference is that AMLO sees
this as a real legal instrument.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:58.120
We are going to govern like this: asking the
people.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.110
They
say that, in order to avoid mistakes, the

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.760
best policy is to

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:02.760
ask.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:03.980
This is democracy!

00:06:03.980 --> 00:06:07.940
It’s not the decision of one man, or
two, or three!...

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.370
Again, the problem is not making referendums.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.990
In fact,
Mexican law already has legislation in place

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:16.520
to regulate how
to make popular consultations.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.560
But, of course, you need an
independent body to run the process and you

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.680
need to reach
a certain turnout.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:26.470
Until this year, 2019, this turnout was 40%
of voters.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:29.120
But, of course, AMLO has already changed this.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:30.970
Now 25% is enough.

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:34.199
25% of Mexican voters is around 20
million people.

00:06:34.199 --> 00:06:38.199
But there are consultations in which less
than 1 million people voted.

00:06:38.199 --> 00:06:41.340
In other words, for AMLO, direct democracy
is pretty

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:43.020
undemocratic.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:44.840
But wait a minute because we aren’t done
yet!

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.180
Apart from consultations... what has AMLO
done in the

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.960
few months he’s been in power?

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.340
Well... he’s been pretty
busy.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:54.930
Let’s check it out, shall we?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:58.400
AMLO WORLD
AMLO’s presidency can be summarized in one

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.639
iconic
gesture.

00:06:59.639 --> 00:07:01.400
Unlike his predecessors, he didn’t want
to live in

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:02.400
the LOS PINOS palace.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.400
You might say, “Oh!

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.400
That’s great!

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.400
A
man of the people, just like JOSE MUJICA in

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.400
Uruguay!”

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.400
But
the question is... where do you think he went

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.400
instead?

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.400
Did
he remain at home?

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.400
Of course he didn’t!

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.400
He went to the
national palace!

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.440
In other words: he just switched one palace
for the other.

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.730
And what do you think he did with the LOS
PINOS palace?

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:18.290
The place has now become a cultural center.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.840
The first big
event was a public screening of ROMA, the

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.070
movie directed
by ALFONSO CUARON, in order to promote Mexican

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.070
movies.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:28.540
And, in this regard, we must admit he was
very

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:29.900
transparent.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:33.750
The ministry of Culture will have to report
how much they

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:37.229
spent in popcorn and punch during the projection
of ROMA

00:07:37.229 --> 00:07:40.449
in LOS PINOS
OK, OK, but let’s be clear here... projecting

00:07:40.449 --> 00:07:44.240
ROMA in the
LOS PINOS palace is not a bad thing.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:46.140
It’s not a good thing
either.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:48.430
But what actually has negative consequences
for the

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:51.840
economy and does scare investors away are
decisions like

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:55.110
cancelling the construction of the airport
and changing all

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:57.520
the deals the previous government had signed
with private

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:58.840
contractors.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:03.690
And this explains news like this.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:06.560
Mexico falls eight positions in the foreign
direct investment

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:07.560
ranking.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.220
Also Mexico fell to the last position in the
ranking

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:11.390
prepared by A.T.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.390
Kearney.

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:13.390
And the same goes for the energy reform.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:16.370
You see, after
decades of having a state monopoly, the Mexican

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:17.370
oil

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.509
company, PEMEX, couldn’t be more corrupt.

00:08:19.509 --> 00:08:22.100
They had an
enormous amount of debt and, if it wasn’t

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.830
for the
Government’s support, they would have gone

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:25.419
bankrupt
years ago.

00:08:25.419 --> 00:08:27.540
The previous president, Peña Nieto, opened
the market for

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.590
foreign investment.

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:32.709
He started by auctioning the smallest oil
fields off to anybody who wanted to exploit

00:08:32.709 --> 00:08:33.709
them.

00:08:33.709 --> 00:08:35.500
The goal
was to increase production and generate more

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.500
money.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.200
The first thing AMLO did as soon as he got
into office was

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.979
freeze all those public auctions.

00:08:39.979 --> 00:08:42.770
He wants Mexico’s oil
industry to remain the way it was.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:45.770
And this is a problem
because the country has a big management issue

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:47.220
in this
regard.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:52.920
For example, even though Mexico has oil reserves,
it imports 70% of its gasoline from the United

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:55.430
States, which
leads to higher gasoline prices.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.190
Why does it import so
much?

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.830
Mainly because PEMEX is so mismanaged that
their

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.850
production falls every year.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.760
And how is AMLO trying to solve this?

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.600
Of course, by
building a brand new refinery!

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.600
The problem?

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.170
PEMEX has
no money and Mexico isn’t growing anymore

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:11.520
so... where is
he going to get the money?

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:22.410
That’s a very good question!

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.820
Mexican Government and Pemex announcement
of building

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:27.620
a new refinery raises many doubts.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:30.440
So far, all the contractors that have been
participating in the

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:34.310
bidding claimed that the conditions the government
requested were not realistic.

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.830
They want the refinery too
early and for too little money.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:39.850
But I guess we will have to
wait until 2022 to see who’s right.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:43.210
But we can already judge the success of the
education

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:44.210
reform.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:50.290
This is another project started by the previous
president that was stopped by AMLO.

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:53.330
In this case, Mexico
had a unique educational system.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:56.010
In most countries,
teachers have to pass an exam in order to

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:58.080
be hired by a
public school.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:09:59.080
Not here!

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:02.310
In this case, it’s the Teacher’s
union that controls the hiring process.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:05.890
And a teaching
position can be SOLD or even INHERITED.

00:10:05.890 --> 00:10:07.560
Yes, you heard
that right.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:10.550
You can inherit a teacher’s job from your
father!

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:12.260
And you don’t even need to prove that you
know the

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:14.570
subjects you’re going to teach!

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:17.000
This is why Mexico changed the system and
introduced a

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:20.290
national exam.

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:24.180
It’s a similar system to Spain’s, for
example.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:27.230
But in Mexico, the change sparked extremely
violent

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.990
protests, especially in the South of the country.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:32.370
Thousands of teachers retired before having
to pass this

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:33.370
exam.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:36.390
And more than a thousand teachers were fired
because, after three attempts, they couldn’t

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:37.390
pass.

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:39.300
Most of
them, of course, got another job at the administration.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:40.300
But don’t worry!

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.300
This is all history!

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:44.430
One of the most vocal
AMLO supporters during the campaign were those

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:45.430
teachers’ unions.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:49.740
So now he’s returning the favour by going
backwards on those reforms.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:51.000
So Mexican teachers will once

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.420
again enjoy their privileges.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:55.600
And Mexican kids will keep
failing all the exams on the PISA report.

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:58.630
But, by far, the most controversial thing
AMLO has done

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:04.600
involves his war against the narcos.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.779
When Mexico was
governed by the right wing, it passed a law

00:11:06.779 --> 00:11:09.040
to allow the
military to fight the narcos.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.370
This definitely didn’t work.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:14.580
In the
last 12 years, Mexico had more than 250,000

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.000
deaths
directly linked to the war on drugs.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.089
AMLO promised he
would stop this war.

00:11:19.089 --> 00:11:20.290
So... what did he do?

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:23.330
Well, instead of using the military...
he’s created a brand new body called the

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.330
NATIONAL
GUARD.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.620
And who’s part of this national guard?

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:27.800
Of course!

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:28.800
Former soldiers!

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:30.779
Even the leader is a former military officer.

00:11:30.779 --> 00:11:33.300
So basically, AMLO changed everything... to
keep

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:34.730
everything the same.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:37.430
And the same is happening with lots of social
programs and

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:38.800
even the Mexico City airport.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:39.959
Yes, we talked about that
before.

00:11:39.959 --> 00:11:42.170
You might think he did that to save money,
right?

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:43.339
Well... not really!

00:11:43.339 --> 00:11:48.530
That money is being reinvested in another
project with a more dubious utility: the MAYAN

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:49.530
TRAIN.

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:51.490
This
train will cross the Southern Mexican states.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:53.589
Which would
be great if those regions were more developed.

00:11:53.589 --> 00:11:56.090
So, with no
people or goods to transport, it’s wishful

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:58.800
thinking to believe
that this is going to push development in

00:11:58.800 --> 00:11:59.800
the region.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:06.020
But this
isn’t even the worse thing!

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:09.640
Mayan organizations ask AMLO to stop the construction
of

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:12.920
the Mayan Train
So far, the project hasn’t passed any of

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.740
the environmental
impact studies.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:17.780
But, still, AMLO’s administration keeps
trying.

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:20.240
In this political climate, where the president
isn’t listening to

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:23.170
anybody, it’s easy to understand why foreign
investors are

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:25.350
leaving the country by the dozens.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:28.540
And this has already had
an impact on the country’s economic growth.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.730
So now the
question goes to you.

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:33.589
Do you think AMLO will manage to avoid a recession
in

00:12:33.589 --> 00:12:34.589
Mexico?

00:12:34.589 --> 00:12:35.640
Or do you think the money that’s running
away

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:37.840
from the country will never come back?

